    "summary": "Man&#039;s gown (tobe, boubou, riga). The body is composed of 119 narrow strips of hand-spun white cotton hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The strips in the tunic are sewn vertically, while those of the sleeves are sewn horizontally and are of uneven length so that they flare out towards the top. A square pocket has been sewn onto the front of the tunic. The pocket, shouloder and front are hand-embroidered in green thread with the &#039;eight knives&#039; pattern (aska takwas) in satin and buttonhole eyelet stitch. The tunic is hemmed around the neck, sleeves and base.",
